<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23834" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insĭdĭātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				soldier lying in ambush</i>, <i><span class="en">Hirt.
				B. G. 8, 18</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>one who lies in
				wait</i>, <i>a lurker</i>, <i>waylayer</i> (rare but class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cat. 2, 12, 27</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in foro collocatur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Mil. 7, 19</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imperii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nep. Reg.
					2</span></i>
			.</div>
